# ADR Candidates

Use this file for consequential decisions that are known to matter but aren't yet framed clearly enough to draft an ADR. This is a step before [../../open/OPEN_DECISIONS.md](../../open/OPEN_DECISIONS.md), which assumes the options are already framed and only needs a yes/no.

This is opt-in — most projects can go straight from a discussion to a drafted ADR and never need a staging area. Copy this file into `docs/adr/` only once undecided architectural questions start accumulating faster than they can be framed.

## Status Values

| Status | Meaning |
| --- | --- |
| `Candidate` | Needs framing before an ADR is drafted. |
| `Proposed` | ADR draft exists but is not accepted. |
| `Accepted` | Decision is recorded in an accepted ADR. |
| `Deferred` | Decision is recognized but not ready to make. |
| `Superseded` | Decision was replaced by a later ADR. |

